If you're running from the MinGW\bin directory, then you aren't following
the instructions which explicitly state that you build from the NetHack
src directory.

> *sigh* There isn't any way to use MinGW without using the command
> prompt, is there?  I really don't like that thing.  I was raised on
> Windows, it intimidates me :(

You could save all of the following lines to a file called
nhbuild.bat and double-click on it:

REM ------------- Start of NHBUILD.BAT ----------------
@echo on
set nhtop=C:\nethack-3.4.3
set mingwtop=C:\MinGW\bin

set _savepath=%PATH%
set PATH=%mingwtop%;%_savepath%
pushd %nhtop%

Rem Step 11
cd sys\winnt

Rem Step 12
call .\nhsetup.bat

Rem Turn echo back on
@echo on

Rem Step 13
cd ..\..\src

Rem Step 15
mingw32-make -f Makefile.gcc install

Rem Cleanup
set PATH=%_savepath%
popd

Echo Your NetHack executable should be %nhtop%\binary\nethack.exe
Echo Press Return
Pause
REM ------------- End of NHBUILD.BAT ----------------

